senses.gloss:
(I)--a sage who called on भीष्म lying on his death-bed; also called on परिक्षित् practising प्रायोप- वेश;
1: भा. I. 9. 7; १९. 9.
was invited for युधिष्ठिर's राजसूय;
2: Ib. X. ७४. 7.
came to see कृष्ण at स्यमन्तपञ्चक;
3: Ib. X. ८४. 4.
one of the sages who left for पिण्डारक.
4: Ib. XI. 1. १२.

(III)--a siddha;
1: भा. VI. १५. १३.
the आचार्य of श्राद्ध deva. Finding no issue to him. वसिष्ठ offered a sacrifice to Mitra and वरुण. At this time श्राद्धा, [page३-167+ ३४] the king's wife desired to have a daughter and expressed it to the होता who uttered the मन्त्र in such a way as to get a daughter. इला was born; but श्राद्धदेव was not pleased. So वसिष्ठ converted इला into a male by name Sudyumna;
2: Ib. IX. 1. १३-22, ३६-7; M. २४५. ८६.
was present at अम्बरीष's अस्वमेध;
3: भा. IX. 4. २२.
the ideal पुरोहीत.
4: Ib. XI. १६. २२.

(XII)--a son of उत्तानपाद: Asked to arbitrate in the dispute involving animal sacrifice; said that यज्ञ involved हिम्स and justified Vasu's action: cursed therefor [page३-171+ २६] by sages to live in रसातल (पाताल-म्।प्।): attained heaven by तपस्;
1: Br. II. ३०. २३-32, ३९ and ४७; ३६. ८९; M. १४३. १८-25. वा. 1. १११; ५७. १०१-11; ६२. ७६.
his daughter अच्छोदामत्स्यगन्धि married परा- शर and gave birth to व्यास;
2: M. १४. १४.
a राजऋषि.
3: वा. ५७. १२२.

--eight in number, and sons of Dharma and Vasu;
1: भा. VI. 6. १०; 7. 2; १०. १७; Br. II. ३८. 2; IV. १५. २४.
worshipped for wealth;
2: भा. II. 3. 3; IX. २४. ५३; Vi. III. 1. ३१.
fought with कालेयस् in a देवासुर war; gods of the Vaivasvata epoch, who wait on Hari;
3: भा. VIII. १०. ३४; १३. 4; IX. २४. ५२; X. ३९. ५४.
came with other gods to द्वारका to ask कृष्ण to go to वैकुण्ठ.
4: Ib. XI. 6. 2; १६. १३.
Brothers of साध्यस् and cursed to experi- ence birth by sexual union; vanquished by रावण; their overlord was Agni;
5: Br. II. २७. २४; III. 3. २० and ८०; 7. २५४; 8. 5; M. 8. 4; Vi. I. २२. 3; V. 1. १७; 4. 5.
also ज्योतिष्मन्तस् and व्यापकस्;
6: M. 5. १७; Vi. I. 9. ६४ and ७०; १५. १०५.
one of the seven classes of deities of the Vaivasvata epoch;
7: M. 9. २९.
eight in number considered as अम्शा of वासुदेव;
8: Ib. 5. २०-21; २५. ४३; ३६. 1; ५२. २१; वा. १०. ७१; ३९, ४९; ३०. ८३, ९९; ६४. 2; ६६. १९; ६९. ४४; १०६. ५९; १०९. २२; Vi. I. १५. १०९-10.
पितृस् said to be Vasus;
9: M. १९. 3.
Somapas.
१०: Ib. ६९. ६२; १३२. 3; २०३. 3; २४६. ६०; २४७. ११.
